<h2 id="as-link" class="doc-h2">As Link</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    shadcn writes <code>&lt;Button asChild&gt;&lt;Link href&gt;</code>, which needs
    <code>cloneElement</code>. Give it an <code>Href</code> instead and it renders a real
    <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> — so middle-click opens a tab, the status bar shows where it goes, and
    Unpoly follows it.
</p>
<Example Source="ButtonAsLink.razor"><ButtonAsLink /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">RTL</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Nothing to configure. Every spacing and border class in the library is a logical property, so
    <code>dir="rtl"</code> on an ancestor is the whole story — the icon moves to the other side of
    the label because <code>gap</code> follows the writing direction.
</p>
<Example Source="ButtonRtl.razor"><ButtonRtl /></Example>
